Terraform Commands for day to day workflow

 1. terraform --version – Check Terraform version 
 2. terraform init – Initialize Terraform working directory 
 3. terraform plan – Show execution plan 
 4. terraform apply -auto-approve – Apply configuration 
 5. terraform destroy -auto-approve – Destroy infrastructure 
 6. terraform show – Show Terraform state 
 7. terraform validate – Validate Terraform configuration
 8. terraform fmt – Format Terraform code 
 9. terraform providers – List providers used 
10. terraform state list – Show managed resources 
11. terraform state show resource_name – Show specific resource details 
12. terraform state rm resource_name – Remove resource from state 
13. terraform taint resource_name – Mark resource for recreation 
14. terraform untaint resource_name – Remove taint from resource 
15. terraform import resource_type.name id – Import existing infrastructure 16. terraform refresh – Refresh state file 
17. terraform graph – Generate dependency graph 
18. terraform workspace list – List available workspaces 
19. terraform workspace select workspace_name – Switch workspace 
20. terraform workspace new workspace_name – Create new workspace 
21. terraform state mv old_resource new_resource – Rename resource 
22. terraform output – Show Terraform outputs 
23. terraform output output_name – Get specific output value 
24. terraform apply -target=resource_name – Apply specific resource 
25. terraform console – Open interactive Terraform shell 
26. terraform debug – Enable debugging logs 
27. terraform version – Show installed Terraform version 
28. terraform plan -var="instance_type=t2.micro" – Pass variable via CLI 
29. terraform apply -var-file="vars.tfvars" – Apply using variable file 
30. terraform apply -auto-approve – Skip manual approval 
31. terraform workspace delete workspace_name – Delete workspace 
32. terraform plan -detailed-exitcode – Get exit codes for changes 
33. terraform force-unlock LOCK_ID – Unlock Terraform state 
34. terraform state push – Manually push state file 
35. terraform state pull – Download current state file 
36. terraform output -json – Get output in JSON format 
37. terraform fmt -recursive – Format Terraform in subdirectories 
38. terraform destroy -target=resource_name – Destroy specific resource 
39. terraform show -json – Show JSON output 
40. terraform validate -no-color – Validate without
